> Whi is big XP bad?

As your XP level rises, more difficult creatures are generated.  Most
people consider the benefits for a higher XP to be outweighed by this
drawback, especially for non-spellcasters.

I always thought this was kind of silly, since it's so
counterintuitive.  It's one of those strategies that you'd only know
about if you were spoiled, which reinforces the whole notion that
Nethack is a game built for spoiled players more than anything.  You
could get rid of the "XP is bad" effect by placing a greater emphasis
on dungeon level and less on player level.

